<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #070d1e; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Kadiri</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Destination Delivery Handover Procedure for Two‑Wheeler & Motorcycle</h3>
<p>The handover at the final destination is a critical control point that confirms the vehicle has arrived in the same condition as it left the origin. The process is standardized to protect both the transporter and the recipient, and it consists of three inter‑linked stages: daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification, and a signed condition sign‑off.</p>
<p>Each stage is documented and cross‑checked against the original pickup records to eliminate disputes and ensure transparency.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Conduct the visual inspection under natural daylight to reveal any surface damage, scratches, dents, or missing components that may be hidden under artificial lighting.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the vehicle’s current appearance with the high‑resolution pickup photographs taken at the point of origin. Note any discrepancies and photograph them for the handover record.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Use a standardized checklist that covers bodywork, lights, mirrors, tires, chain/belt tension, and any accessories that were part of the original load.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Document the findings in a written condition report, highlighting both “as‑received” and “as‑delivered” observations.</span></li>
    </ul>
</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Verification Against the LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Read the odometer on the vehicle and record the exact mileage at the delivery point.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Cross‑reference this reading with the mileage noted on the Lorry Receipt (LR) bilty, which captures the odometer at the time of pickup.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If a variance greater than the allowable tolerance (typically 5 km) is detected, investigate possible causes such as route detours, idle time, or tampering before proceeding.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Enter the verified mileage in the handover log and attach a copy of the LR bilty for audit purposes.</span></li>
    </ul>
</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Present the completed condition report, the photographic comparison, and the odometer verification sheet to the recipient.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both the transporter’s representative and the recipient must sign and date the document, confirming that the vehicle has been inspected, that the mileage matches the LR bilty, and that they accept the vehicle in its current state.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Provide the recipient with a copy of the signed handover form; retain the original for the carrier’s records.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Any noted damages or mileage discrepancies are now formally acknowledged, reducing the risk of future claims.</span></li>
    </ul>
</span></li>
</ul>
<p>By rigorously following these three steps—daylight re‑inspection, odometer verification, and signed sign‑off—both parties achieve a clear, documented transfer of responsibility, ensuring that the two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its final destination exactly as expected.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
